&lt;div class="WordSection4"&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-top: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; page-break-after: avoid; border: none; mso-padding-alt: 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt; mso-border-shadow: yes;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE 4. PENSION PLANS AND OTHER POSTRETIREMENT BENEFIT PLANS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-top: 6.0pt; line-height: 120%; border: none; mso-padding-alt: 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt; mso-border-shadow: yes;"&gt;The Company contributed $7 million in cash to the pension plan during the six months ended June 30, 2026. The Company expects to contribute $10 million in total in 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%; page-break-after: avoid; border: none; mso-padding-alt: 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt; mso-border-shadow: yes; margin: 6.0pt 0in 6.0pt 0in;"&gt;The Company uses a December 31 measurement date for its defined benefit pension and other postretirement benefit plans. The following table sets forth the components of net periodic benefit costs for the three and six months ended June 30 (dollars in millions):&lt;/p&gt;
